-# FOOLISH ARC — Repair, Verification & Fit Finder Integration Notes
+# FOOLISH ARC security audit and repair notes
 
-This document summarizes all repairs, security upgrades, regression test fixes, and Fit Finder integrations completed in this production-ready source package.
+The source ZIP includes FIXES.diff, an exact patch against the original project. Apply it only to an unmodified original. The source files in this ZIP already contain the changes.
 
-## 1. All 90 Original Regression Tests + 8 New Security & Fit Finder Tests Passing (98 / 98 Passed)
+## Findings and corrections
 
-- **Resolved all 33 previously failing regression tests**:
-  - Restored the complete FORME signature catalog (`forme-01` through `forme-14`) alongside the Men's and Women's Denim & Pret collections in `src/data/products.js` and `server/seedData.js`.
-  - Added the Kids' collection (`forme-13`, `forme-14`) with age-bracket sizing (`4–5`, `6–7`, `8–9`, `10–11`) and child mannequin scaling (`translate(0 118) scale(1 .82)`).
-  - Standardized adult sizing (`XS`, `S`, `M`, `L`, `XL` alongside numeric waist sizes) so both Fitting Room ensembles and product pages work seamlessly.
-  - Added automated suite `tests/e2e/tier1_features/f17_security_and_fit_finder.test.js` covering the Fit Finder rules engine, measurement log redaction, CSRF token verification, persistent customer JWT sessions, OAuth 2.0 PKCE generation, and rate limiting.
-  - Run `npm test` (or `node --test tests/e2e/tier1_features/*.test.js`) to verify **98 passed, 0 failed**.
+| Area | Finding | Implemented correction |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Application startup | The React build and API imports referenced five absent modules. The original 90 tests passed without starting either application. | Restored the Fit Finder engine, dialog, data models and rate limiter. Added tests against the live Express API. |
+| Checkout | A standalone-database fallback could reserve stock without saving the order. The customer update targeted the same history field with two conflicting operators. | Required MongoDB transactions for multi-document order changes, corrected the history update, and bound idempotency replays to the submitted request. An order retry after a page refresh can reuse a session-scoped reference. |
+| Owner and customer sessions | Administrator writes could accept a content-type header alone. Development signing used a public hard-coded fallback. | Used the installed JWT library with restricted algorithm, issuer, audience and expiry. Bound the owner CSRF token to the signed session. Development uses a random per-process secret. Production needs an explicit signing secret. |
+| Google sign-in | The redirect handler did not enforce its stored state. Access tokens could be accepted without checking the intended client. | Required a one-time state and cryptographic S256 PKCE. Restricted callback addresses. Checked Google-issued identity and client audience on the server, and bound returning accounts to the Google subject. |
+| Measurements and contact data | Caller-selected guest profile identifiers and browser caches exposed sensitive data on shared devices. Failed saves and deletions could appear successful. | Scoped guest access to a random HTTP-only cookie, stored a digest of the token and isolated account profiles. Measurements are saved on explicit request. Sensitive historical browser caches are cleared. |
+| Web requests and rendering | Public write endpoints lacked effective throttling. Catalog fields could inject markup into a fitting-room SVG. | Bounded request sizes and rate-limit memory, limited accepted content types, validated SVG attributes, added security headers for Express and Vercel, and limited receipt sizes and checked their file signatures. |
+| Dependencies | The original lockfile reported high-severity advisories for Joi and body-parser. | Updated the lockfile and constrained the affected versions. The final npm audit reported zero known dependency vulnerabilities. |
 
-## 2. Security & Architecture Upgrades Completed
+## Storefront changes
 
-- **Explicit CSRF & Origin Defense (`server/middleware/auth.js`, `server/index.js`, `src/services/api.js`)**:
-  - Owner login (`/api/auth/login`) and session verification (`/api/auth/verify`) issue an HMAC-signed CSRF token (`foolisharc_csrf`).
-  - Every state-changing admin request (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`) verifies `Origin`/`Referer` allow-lists and `X-CSRF-Token` / `X-Requested-With` headers via `verifyStateChangingRequestCsrf`.
-- **Persistent Authenticated Customer Sessions (`server/middleware/auth.js`, `server/index.js`)**:
-  - Customer sign-in (`/api/auth/google-client`, `/api/auth/google-code`, `/api/auth/set-password`, `/api/auth/client-login`) now issues an HTTP-only signed JWT cookie (`foolisharc_customer`, 7-day expiry) verified via `GET /api/auth/customer-session` and cleared via `POST /api/auth/customer-logout`.
-- **OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code + PKCE Flow (`src/utils/googleAuth.js`, `src/pages/GoogleAuthCallbackPage.jsx`, `server/index.js`)**:
-  - Replaced the legacy `response_type=token` implicit redirect helper with cryptographic **Authorization Code + PKCE** (`response_type=code`, `code_challenge`, `code_challenge_method=S256`) and server-side code exchange at `POST /api/auth/google-code`, while retaining the Google Identity Services (GIS) popup flow.
-- **Distributed / Shared Rate Limiter (`server/middleware/rateLimiter.js`)**:
-  - Supports distributed Redis REST (`UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` and `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`) or a custom store adapter, with automatic in-memory fallback and standard `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, and `Retry-After` headers.
-- **Graceful MongoDB Transaction Fallback (`server/index.js`)**:
-  - `runWithOptionalTransaction()` runs checkout (`POST /api/orders`), customer cancellation (`POST /api/orders/:orderNumber/cancel`), and admin status updates (`PATCH /api/orders/:id/status`) inside a snapshot transaction on MongoDB Atlas replica sets, and automatically falls back to atomic conditional `$gte` stock updates if run against a standalone local MongoDB instance.
+Collection links open the requested department. Search, in-stock size filtering, sorting, saved garments and garment-type filters work together. The redesigned page uses supplied editorial photography and adapts to mobile screens. Fit Finder matches body measurements to a garment chart and reports when there is no match. Quick selection, the non-empty bag, the fitting-room route, stock display and order tracking were repaired. Storefront, checkout and server share the same shipping calculation. The admin receipt image is fetched on demand.
 
-## 3. Integrated Fit Finder Suite (White `#FAF8F5`, Camel `#C69F6F` & Subtle Black `#141413`)
+## Verification
 
-- **Deterministic Rules Engine (`src/engine/fitFinderEngine.js`)**:
-  - Per-product `sizeChart`, `fitType` (`slim` | `regular` | `relaxed`), `fitAdjustment` (`-1`, `-0.5`, `0`, `0.5`, `1`), `hasStretch`, and `fitNotes`.
-  - Height/weight anthropometric lookup table + optional exact Chest/Waist/Hip override, body shape modifiers, tie handling (`Between sizes`), metric/imperial sanity check, and honest out-of-range detection.
-- **Backend Endpoints & Privacy (`server/index.js`, `server/models/FitProfile.js`, `server/models/FitFeedback.js`)**:
-  - `POST /api/fit/recommend`, `POST /api/fit/profile` (consent-gated, blocked when `shoppingForSomeoneElse` is enabled), `GET /api/fit/profile`, `DELETE /api/fit/profile`, `POST /api/fit/feedback` (post-delivery WhatsApp feedback loop), and `PUT /api/products/:id/fit` (owner calibration).
-  - Server logs automatically redact body measurements via `redactMeasurements()`.
-- **Storefront Placements (`src/components/FitFinderModal.jsx`, `src/pages/ProductDetailPage.jsx`, `src/components/CartDrawer.jsx`, `src/components/Navbar.jsx`)**:
-  - **Product Page**: Inline `"Recommended for you"` badge on the recommended size button, auto-selection when a saved profile exists, and a `"Find my size"` trigger right under the size buttons (never opens on page load).
-  - **Cart Drawer**: Displays `"You usually fit M in this cut"` with a 1-click `"Switch to M"` action when a cart item's selected size differs from the customer's recommendation.
-  - **Header**: `"My fit profile"` button in the top navigation bar to view, edit, or delete saved measurements at any time.
+- The production Vite build completed on Node 24.
+- The 98 standard regression and API tests passed. Run them with `npm test`.
+- A separate MongoDB 7.0 replica-set integration test passed. It covers rollback after a missing item, concurrent retries, server pricing, cross-request replay rejection, email-gated tracking, concurrent cancellation and guest profile isolation. To repeat, set `TEST_MONGODB_URI` to a disposable replica set and run `npm run test:db`. The test creates and removes its own database.
+- A Chromium test selected a department and available size, typed a product search, applied a Fit Finder suggestion, placed a guest cash-on-delivery order, checked the bag cleared, and opened the tracked order. The collection was checked at 390 and 1365 pixels.
+- No real customer data, provider accounts or payment transfers were used. Live Google sign-in, SMTP/Resend delivery, manual-payment settlement and production hosting still need verification with deployment credentials.
+- Rate limits are per server process. Set platform-level limits for deployments with multiple instances. Set TRUST_PROXY to a trusted address or CIDR when self-hosting behind a proxy. Existing database catalog records are retained; seed-photo and stock corrections apply to a newly seeded catalog.
